---
import Shell from '../components/Martlet.astro';import {localPath as href} from '../paths';
const page={id:'language',toc:[{id:'relationships',title:'Relationships'},{id:'hierarchy',title:'Hierarchy'},{id:'states',title:'States and continuity'},{id:'boundaries',title:'Boundaries'}],title:'A language worth keeping.',eyebrow:'Martlet · Principles',summary:'A wide document tests the shared masthead, index, reading measure, and typography.'};
---
<Shell page={page} href={href} base={import.meta.env.BASE_URL} renderContent={false}><h2 id="relationships">Relationships</h2><p>Start with proximity: a label and its control, related fields, and distinct tasks need different amounts of space. Let readable sequence do the work before adding containers.</p><h2 id="hierarchy">Hierarchy</h2><p>A title names the page. Metadata explains its context. Section headings divide the argument. Controls should look like controls, and sustained prose should have a bounded reading measure.</p><table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Object</th><th scope="col">Responsibility</th></tr></thead><tbody>{[['Masthead','Title, summary, date, author, and tags'],['Navigation','Links to other destinations'],['Contents','Links into the current document'],['Reading column','The argument and its evidence']].map(([name,purpose])=><tr><th scope="row">{name}</th><td>{purpose}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table><h2 id="states">States and continuity</h2><p>Appearance is a page preference, not a replacement for semantic structure. Light and dark retain the same relationships. The menu exposes its expanded state, responds to Escape, and returns focus to its trigger.</p><blockquote>A shared stylesheet is a contract between markup and presentation. It is not a promise that unrelated markup will look the same.</blockquote><h2 id="boundaries">Boundaries</h2><p>These templates borrow no institutional or personal content from the source websites. Their shell is a maintained derivative of the canonical reference. The original websites remain unchanged.</p><p><a href={href('/examples/dashboard-components/')}>Explore the component inventory</a> and <a href={href('/documentation/')}>native documentation layout</a>.</p></Shell>
